      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_a",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in paragraph (a), by deleting the word “and” at the end of the paragraph;"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_a__subpara_ii",
      "@type": "akn:subparagraph",
      "eli:number": "ii",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_a",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in paragraph (b), by substituting for the full stop at the end of the paragraph the words “; and”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_a__subpara_iii",
      "@type": "akn:subparagraph",
      "eli:number": "iii",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_a",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after paragraph (b) the following paragraph: “(c) the granting of recognition to any other training programmes under section 36a.”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_4",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (5), in the national language text, by substituting for the words “Penolong Kanan Pengarah” the words “Penolong Pengarah Kanan”. Amendment of section 24"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "5",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_b",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_c"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 24 of the principal Act is amended—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (1), by substituting for the words “its training programme” the words “its skills training programme”;"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (5), by inserting after the words “or any officer of the department responsible for skills development” the words “or any other person appointed by the Director General”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5__para_c",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "c",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_5",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection: “(6) A skills training provider shall be disqualified from applying for the accreditation of a skills training programme under subsection (1) if the skills training provider has an existing accredited programme in respect of which the certificate of accreditation has been suspended or revoked by the Director General under section 29 or 32, as the case may be, and a period of one year from the effective date of such suspension or revocation has not lapsed.”. Amendment of section 25"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_6",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "6",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Paragraph 25(1)(a) of the principal Act is amended by substituting for the words “three years” the words “not more than six years”. Amendment of section 27"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_7",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "7",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Paragraph 27(2)(a) of the principal Act is amended by substituting for the words “three years” the words “not more than six years”. Amendment of section 29"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_8",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "8",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 29 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsections: “(3) Upon receipt of the written notice under subsection (2), the skills training provider may make written representations to the Director General within thirty days from the date of the receipt of the notice, stating the reasons why the certificate of accreditation in respect of the accredited programme should not be suspended or revoked. (4) After the expiry of the period of thirty days specified in subsection (3) or after considering any written representations made, the Director General may— (a) issue a warning and give directions to the skills training provider for the skills training provider to rectify, to the satisfaction of the Director General, the matter in respect of which the proposed suspension or revocation relates; or (b) proceed with the proposed action to suspend or revoke the certificate of accreditation. (5) If the skills training provider fails to rectify the matter as required under paragraph (4)(a), the Director General may proceed to suspend or revoke the certificate of accreditation. (6) A written notice of the decision of the Director General to suspend or revoke the certificate of accreditation shall be served to the skills training provider if the action of suspension or revocation is imposed under paragraph (4)(b) or subsection (5). (7) The suspension or revocation of the certificate of accreditation under this section shall take effect on the date specified by the Director General in the written notice served under subsection (6).”. Substitution of section 34"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@/~cl_9",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "9",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/35/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by substituting for section 34 the following section: “Award of Certificate 34. (1) The Director General may award a Certificate to any person who has conformed to the Standards in respect of the following skills qualifications: (a) Malaysian Skills Certificate; (b) Malaysian Skills Diploma; (c) Malaysian Skills Advanced Diploma; (d) Malaysian Modular Skills Certificate; or (e) Statements of Achievement. (2) The Director General may award a Certificate to any person who has conformed to the Standards in respect of the following skills recognitions: (a) Skills Expert; (b) Senior Skills Expert; or (c) Skills Consultant.”. New Part VIIa"
      }
    }
  ]
}
